%% Azure Migrate appliance over Private Link - project creation, DNS proof, registration and first replication, with the name-resolution failure branch - Contoso profile
%% Source: codex/blueprint-azure-migrate-private-link-landing.md and codex/playbook-azure-migrate-private-link-cache-storage.md; Microsoft Learn "Migrate servers to Azure by using Private Link" and "Troubleshoot network connectivity issues - Azure Migrate"
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant OPS as eng-netops
  participant PORTAL as Azure portal or REST
  participant PROJ as Migrate project plus Key Vault, usage storage and Recovery Services vault
  participant ZONE as privatelink zones in the project resource group
  participant IB as Infoblox grid
  participant RES as DNS Private Resolver inbound endpoint in the hub
  participant APP as Migrate appliance on Contoso network
  participant CACHE as Contoso cache storage account
  OPS->>PORTAL: create the project with connectivity method Private endpoint
  Note over OPS,PORTAL: PowerShell cannot create a private-link project, and the connectivity method is immutable afterwards
  PORTAL->>PROJ: generate the appliance key
  PROJ->>ZONE: Azure creates Key Vault, the usage storage account and the vault, attaches a private endpoint to each and writes the zones
  OPS->>PROJ: Download DNS settings from BOTH properties pages
  PROJ-->>OPS: the FQDN and private IP pairs that are the oracle for this project
  OPS->>IB: conditional forwarders for the four privatelink zones to the resolver inbound endpoint
  Note over OPS,IB: forward the privatelink zones only, never all of core.windows.net, and link or merge the Migrate zones rather than duplicating them on the VNet
  OPS->>CACHE: create the GPv2 cache account with a blob private endpoint, keep bypass AzureServices
  OPS->>CACHE: grant the vault managed identity Contributor and Storage Blob Data Contributor
  APP->>IB: resolve every FQDN from the settings file
  IB->>RES: forwarded query for the privatelink name
  RES->>ZONE: lookup in the linked zone
  ZONE-->>APP: A record 10.x.x.x
  alt every name matches the private IP in the settings file
    APP->>PROJ: register with the project key over TCP 443 through the project private endpoint
    PROJ-->>APP: registration complete, discovery starts, no AgentNotConnected
    APP->>CACHE: replication writes through the blob private endpoint
    CACHE-->>OPS: Data Bytes In on the endpoint increases - this metric is the closure evidence
  else a name answers with a public IP or NXDOMAIN
    APP-->>OPS: AgentNotConnected, ForbiddenToAccessKeyVault, or a 504 while saving the appliance configuration
    OPS->>IB: add the missing forwarder, or delete the duplicate zone that holds no record
    OPS->>APP: remove the hosts-file entries left from testing and add proxy bypass rules for every privatelink FQDN
    Note over OPS,APP: the hosts file is a documented testing-only fallback and must be empty at go-live
    OPS->>APP: retry the DNS proof, then registration
  end
  APP-->>OPS: portal, Entra ID, management.azure.com, aka.ms and download.microsoft.com stay on the public path - no forwarder makes these legs private
